It would appear certain monster types are not affected by extinction 
(or genocide?) on the Quest levels. In particular, those guaranteed to 
be generated on some levels - for the Knight quest that includes 
quasits and ochre jellies. I've not found the code that deals with 
Quest monster generation. Would this be considered a bug? I can imagine 
the DevTeam not wanting Quest nasties to be genocided, but why not 
rendered extinct?

How do I know this? I've spent a great deal of time (ahem) altar 
camping on the Quest locate level, including burning up the numerous 
magic traps. In spite of having slaughtered many, many quasits they 
still kept on coming. Wandering what was up, I copied the save game 
file (shock! horror! controversy!), loaded the copy and quit, only 
asking for a list of monsters vanquished. Lo and behold, 255 dead 
quasits and 255 dead ochre jellies. With quasits near 4 times as likely 
to appear as ochre jellies, I'd estimate well in excess of 1000 quasit 
kills. No wonder I was getting suspicious. Lugh must be sick of sacced 
quasits by now.

Other i and j are at (near enough) 120 kills, so they have probably 
